# Validation coverage

What this report establishes, and what it does not. Both tables are built from the same
acceptance log as the verdict, so neither can claim coverage the report did not deliver: a
parameter the package starts producing appears as NOT COVERED until some scenario compares
it, and a capability whose scenario fails to report is shown as such instead of being taken
on trust.

Three kinds of evidence are distinguished throughout, and they are not interchangeable:

| Kind | What it establishes | Where it comes from |
|---|---|---|
| external | agreement with an independent implementation | Phoenix WinNonlin 8.0, Appendix 2 |
| analytic | agreement with an exact closed form | the integration-rules chapter |
| internal | that the behaviour has not changed | a value fixed by this package itself |

An internal baseline is **not** evidence of correctness. It exists only where no external
reference can be had, and the report says so at the point of use.

## Parameters

```julia; echo = false, results = "tex"

# The parameters the package actually produced during this build. Collected by
# running the configurations rather than listed by hand, so a parameter added to
# the package shows up here on the next build without anyone remembering to add
# it.
producible = Set{Symbol}()
dsc = MetidaNCA.pkimport(pkdata2, :Time, :Concentration, [:Subject, :Formulation])
# The dose time matters here as much as the method: with dosetime 0 the first
# observation of this data set is zero, so Cmin is zero and the parameters that
# divide by it (Swing) are not produced at all. A configuration with a non-zero
# dose time is included so that they are listed.
for (a, cm, dtm, tau) in ((:ev, :lint, 0.0, nothing), (:ev, :luld, 0.0, 12.0),
                          (:iv, :lint, 0.0, 12.0),    (:ev, :logt, 0.0, 12.0),
                          (:ev, :luldt, 0.0, 12.0),   (:iv, :luld, 0.0, nothing),
                          (:ev, :luld, 0.25, 9.0),    (:iv, :luld, 0.25, 9.0))
    dtc = isnothing(tau) ? MetidaNCA.DoseTime(dose = 100, time = dtm) :
                           MetidaNCA.DoseTime(dose = 100, time = dtm, tau = tau)
    MetidaNCA.setdosetime!(dsc, dtc)
    for r in MetidaNCA.nca!(dsc; adm = a, calcm = cm)
        union!(producible, keys(r.result))
    end
end
for r in MetidaNCA.nca!(upkp); union!(producible, keys(r.result)); end
union!(producible, keys(MetidaNCA.nca!(pdp).result))

print(mdtable(acceptance_coverage_table(collect(producible))))
```
Table: Coverage of every parameter produced during this build

```julia; echo = false, results = "tex"
print(acceptance_coverage_summary(collect(producible)))
```

